{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1387137-gaian-answer-to-level-6-rite-of-the-vengeful-spider","id":1387137,"title":"Gaian answer to Level 6 Rite of the Vengeful Spider?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-09T18:05:28-07:00","id":1387137,"title":"Gaian answer to Level 6 Rite of the Vengeful Spider?","content":"I've been thinking about the Apocalypse book, and how the Shadowlords tried to help their totem ascend by performing an impossible task in a year's time. I also remember the Rite of the Vengeful Spider, a Level 6 Rite designed to take out a Tribal totem. I want to eventually do a Level 6 Rite, something that will finish off chronicle with a bang. The idea is that it will either be the Shadowlords ultimate ploy to take control of the Garou Nation, or the Silver Fangs attempt to redeem themselves of their failures. Not necessarily something to take out Whippoorwill, but maybe a way to either take out the BSD tribe or at least giving some of the lower ranking BSDs a chance to redeem themselves by shifting sideways into the Erebus. But I'm really having a hard time designing such a Rite. Obviously you would be tempting 5 Elder Black Spiral Dancers, each of a different Auspice back to Gaia, but beyond that I'm still brainstorming ideas. Anyone have some ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T04:37:30-07:00","id":1387247,"title":"","content":"I'd probably start with the Rite of Still Skies as inspiration for a new Gaian Rite to do something that big (it's the legendary Rite that was used to bind Storm Eater).<br /> <br /> Esp. since Still Skies is a binding, rather than destruction focused Rite, it would work well for something like smacking the vast majority of BSDs with a mystic imperative to go to Erebus, or suffer a significant curse (like not being able to regain Rage and Gnosis) until they do.<br /> <br /> Still Skies also focuses on the Gaian Garou making a huge sacrifice of their own to make it happen (and one that could have easily gone to waste considering the coordination required, and how hard it is to find such sacrifices given they're willing Rank 6 Garou). So that might work if you want the Silver Fangs to take the hit as a redemption bit (it can even be a Shadow Lord influenced thing since they could try to con the Fangs into thinking one Tribe has to shoulder the burden instead of Still Skies everyone has to sacrifice one, when that's not really true, in the hopes that it would weaken the Fangs enough for the Lords to take over).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}